    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a proposal for a new high-density residential complex in an older part of the city. I need to prep for a community meeting and I want to know what the main criticisms against high-density zoning usually are. Can you give me a breakdown of the arguments people use to oppose these kinds of developments? I want to make sure I'm not blindsided.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Common criticisms of high-density development often include concerns about increased traffic congestion, strain on limited public infrastructure like schools and parks, and the potential loss of neighborhood character. Opponents frequently argue that such growth can lower property values, create monopolies on local employment, and negatively impact the local tax base. Additionally, there is often fear regarding the \"crime\" factor and the displacement of existing residents due to higher land values. Being prepared to address these specific social and economic aspects will help you effectively communicate the project's long-term benefits.",
